# Run logs are experiment data, not source. Out of git by default...
runs/*.jsonl
runs/smoke-state.json

# ...except the probe runs RESEARCH_LOG.md actually cites. They are the evidence
# for its claims, and committing them means anyone can load them in the replay
# viewer and check the engine reproduces every recorded step.
# Archived engine directories are not matched by the single-level glob above,
# so everything under runs/archive-engine-*/ is committed as-is.
!runs/codex-v4-2026-09-19T1208.jsonl
.env
.env.local

# scratch files used to compose commit messages
.msg.txt
.e11.md
